WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
We define artificial intelligence as a
specific field of computer science

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.600
focused on building systems that simulate
human perception, reasoning,

3
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.840
and decision-making. The theoretical
foundation of this field stretches back

4
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:18.760
to the 1950s, catalyzed by Alan Turing and
his proposals for testing machine

5
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.940
intelligence. But the early decades of
expert systems often resulted in unmet

6
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.700
expectations. The explosive growth we are
seeing today, which took off in the

7
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.980
2010s, is driven by massive data sets and
raw computing power.
